  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ASEAN USAID Partnership Program</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN)):  .The ASEAN USAID Partnership Program is a demand-driven and.flexible program to advance shared priorities of the United States and ASEAN.through our Comprehensive Strategic Partnership, which is aligned closely with.the ASEAN Outlook for the Indo-Pacific. The Partnership Program is a key.platform for expanded engagement with ASEAN. Key objectives include supporting.inclusive economic growth, addressing transnational security challenges,.promoting good governance and strengthening capacity of ASEAN institutions. The.Partnership Program will continue working with ASEAN on key issues and emerging.technologies including the ASEAN Artificial Intelligence (AI) Roadmap and.Safety Network, strengthening cybersecurity capacity in the face of increasing.People&apos;s Republic of China (PRC) threats, raising standards in the critical.minerals sector and improving efficiency and volumes of intra-ASEAN and global.trade through the ASEAN Single Window (ASW). These priorities align with 2025.ASEAN Chair Malaysia&apos;s Priority Economic Deliverables. The Partnership Program.will strengthen ASEAN capacity to address key transnational security issues.including Trafficking in Persons (TIP), Preventing and Countering Violent.Extremism (PCVE), building ASEAN&apos;s capacity to respond to natural disasters,.strengthening the region&apos;s health security architecture and continue supporting.disability rights, women&apos;s empowerment and human rights. FY24 funding will.strengthen the capacity of the ASEAN Secretariat and the ASEAN entities to.better address the region&apos;s development challenges, enabling some organizations.to become direct recipients of USAID funding. These ASEAN-affiliated entities.work on diverse issues such as humanitarian assistance, climate change, public.health emergencies, human rights and disabilities. Assistance to ASEAN will.support all member states including high-income countries of Brunei Darussalam.and Singapore..</narrative>
  </description>
